YOLOv26 reverts to a Direct Regression Strategy, removing this module entirely (see Fig. [3](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#S3.F3 "Figure 3 ‣ 3.2 Regression-Centric Decoupled Head (DFL-Free) ‣ 3 Architecture and Methodology of YOLOv26 ‣ YOLO26: An Analysis of NMS-Free End to End Framework for Real-Time Object Detection")). This architectural rollback is motivated by the "Export Gap"—the discrepancy between theoretical FLOPs and actual inference speed on deployed hardware [[34](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib17 "RTMDet: an empirical study of designing real-time object detectors")]. By eliminating the integral representation of Eq. [2](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#S3.E2 "In 3.2 Regression-Centric Decoupled Head (DFL-Free) ‣ 3 Architecture and Methodology of YOLOv26 ‣ YOLO26: An Analysis of NMS-Free End to End Framework for Real-Time Object Detection"), the decoding phase is simplified to a direct linear mapping:

| | | | | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | y^v​26=ℱr​e​g​(x)∈ℝ\hat{y}\_{v26}=\mathcal{F}\_{reg}(x)\in\mathbb{R} | | (3) |

y^v​26=ℱr​e​g​(x)∈ℝ\hat{y}_{v26}=\mathcal{F}_{reg}(x)\in\mathbb{R}

To maintain high precision without the distributional benefits of DFL, YOLOv26 employs a refined Decoupled Head structure inspired by YOLOX [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib27 "YOLOX: exceeding yolo series in 2021")]. As illustrated in standard topologies, the head separates feature extraction into two distinct branches:

| | | | | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | H​e​a​d​(x)={ℱc​l​s​(x),ℱr​e​g​(x)}Head(x)=\{\mathcal{F}\_{cls}(x),\mathcal{F}\_{reg}(x)\} | | (4) |

H​e​a​d​(x)={ℱc​l​s​(x),ℱr​e​g​(x)}Head(x)=\{\mathcal{F}_{cls}(x),\mathcal{F}_{reg}(x)\}

where ℱc​l​s\mathcal{F}\_{cls} predicts class probabilities and ℱr​e​g\mathcal{F}\_{reg} predicts box regression parameters directly. This separation ensures that the removal of DFL does not degrade classification performance [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib27 "YOLOX: exceeding yolo series in 2021")], while the regression branch is optimized via the new STAL and ProgLoss functions to recover the localization precision lost by discarding the distributional prior.

