#### 3.3.3 Progressive Loss Balancing (ProgLoss)

To further stabilize the training of the end-to-end architecture, YOLOv26 employs ProgLoss, a dynamic loss weighting strategy. In standard detectors [[15](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib9 "Ultralytics YOLOv8"), [29](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib21 "Focal loss for dense object detection")], the ratio between classification loss (Lc​l​sL\_{cls}) and bounding box regression loss (Lb​o​xL\_{box}) is typically fixed. However, this static balance is suboptimal for end-to-end learning, where the network must simultaneously learn feature discrimination and precise localization without the geometric guidance of anchor priors [[14](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.12882#bib.bib37 "A curriculum learning approach for object detection")].

